{"format":1,"version":0,"generated_at":"2026-09-26T20:33:24.164Z","exam":{"slug":"jamb","name":"JAMB"},"subject":{"slug":"chemistry","name":"Chemistry","display_name":"Chemistry"},"topics":[],"papers":[{"id":-1,"year":2025,"title":"Chemistry sample questions","duration_minutes":null,"items":[{"id":-30,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the chemical symbol for sodium?</p>","options":{"A":"S","B":"So","C":"Na","D":"Sn"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Sodium comes from its Latin name natrium: Na.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Sodium symbol na Na, from the Latin name natrium.</p>"},{"id":-31,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the formula of water?</p>","options":{"A":"H<sub>2</sub>O","B":"CO<sub>2</sub>","C":"O<sub>2</sub>","D":"NaCl"},"answer":"A","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom: H<sub>2</sub>O.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Two hydrogen and one oxygen: H<sub>2</sub>O.</p>"},{"id":-32,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the pH of a neutral solution?</p>","options":{"A":"0","B":"5","C":"7","D":"14"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>A neutral solution such as pure water has a pH of 7.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Neutral solution like pure water get pH of 7.</p>"},{"id":-33,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Which gas is needed for burning?</p>","options":{"A":"nitrogen","B":"oxygen","C":"helium","D":"argon"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Things burn when they react with oxygen.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Things dey burn wen dem join oxygen.</p>"},{"id":-34,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the atomic number of carbon?</p>","options":{"A":"4","B":"6","C":"8","D":"12"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Carbon has 6 protons, so its atomic number is 6.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Carbon get 6 protons, so atomic number na 6.</p>"},{"id":-35,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Which of these is a noble gas?</p>","options":{"A":"oxygen","B":"chlorine","C":"argon","D":"hydrogen"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Argon is in Group 18, the noble gases.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Argon dey Group 18, the noble gases.</p>"},{"id":-36,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>Iron rusts when it is in contact with</p>","options":{"A":"dry air only","B":"oxygen and water","C":"nitrogen only","D":"oil"},"answer":"B","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Rusting needs both oxygen and water.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Rust need both oxygen and water.</p>"},{"id":-37,"type":"mcq","html":"<p>What is the formula of common salt?</p>","options":{"A":"NaOH","B":"KCl","C":"NaCl","D":"HCl"},"answer":"C","marks":1,"topic_id":null,"explanation_en":"<p>Common salt is sodium chloride: NaCl.</p>","explanation_pcm":"<p>Common salt na sodium chloride: NaCl.</p>"}]}]}